WEBVTT

00:00.940 --> 00:02.560
I feel so hot.

00:02.560 --> 00:04.180
I can't breathe.

00:04.480 --> 00:06.820
My heart is being torn apart.

00:07.240 --> 00:10.500
Blood is rushing wildly inside my body.

00:11.580 --> 00:13.060
How long ago did it happen?

00:13.640 --> 00:16.640
When facing dozens of enemies,

00:16.640 --> 00:19.240
I have felt a similar exhilaration.

00:19.480 --> 00:22.860
But now, it's completely different.

00:23.120 --> 00:26.580
My body started moving on its own.

00:27.400 --> 00:28.580
Why?

00:28.980 --> 00:30.560
What is the reason

00:31.340 --> 00:35.000
that made my body move like that?

00:36.000 --> 00:37.860
I want to understand.

00:43.340 --> 00:45.120
Good morning.

00:47.260 --> 00:49.300
Wow, it's all beautifully packed.

00:49.300 --> 00:52.780
I think it's better to try to
minimize the amount of trash.

00:52.780 --> 00:55.260
So I chopped it all up.

00:55.260 --> 00:58.580
That's impressive, the trash
is half the usual amount.

00:58.580 --> 01:00.320
Thank you, Miss Maid.

01:05.920 --> 01:12.300
(You Are Ms. Servant.)

02:33.750 --> 02:35.640
(Episode 2: I Want to Know You)

02:35.640 --> 02:36.670
It's so brazenly

02:36.670 --> 02:38.400
PLEASE TAKE ME HOME
It's so brazenly

02:38.400 --> 02:40.130
PLEASE TAKE ME HOME
placed at my doorstep.

02:40.580 --> 02:43.080
What do they take my place for?

02:43.080 --> 02:44.360
Master Hitoyoshi.

02:44.360 --> 02:45.940
Here is a letter.

02:47.280 --> 02:50.160
I thought it was a Pomeranian
when I bought it from the pet shop,

02:50.160 --> 02:53.540
but it turned out to be a dog
that will grow big.

02:53.540 --> 02:54.580
I can't keep it at home.

02:54.580 --> 02:57.640
So I put it at the doorstep of
what looks to be a wealthy family.

02:57.640 --> 02:59.220
Please take care of it.

02:59.220 --> 03:00.560
That's so selfish!

03:00.560 --> 03:02.780
And to write about it so lightly,
it's infuriating!

03:03.360 --> 03:04.460
Darn it.

03:04.460 --> 03:07.580
What if my house can't accommodate pets?

03:08.300 --> 03:10.060
Right?

03:11.160 --> 03:12.780
Are you going to keep it?

03:12.780 --> 03:15.500
Eh, I can't just leave it here.

03:15.800 --> 03:17.320
It's so small.

03:17.320 --> 03:20.900
Leaving it outside in summer
could be lethal for it.

03:20.900 --> 03:23.800
And I can't think of anyone else
who could take it in.

03:24.580 --> 03:26.080
Even though it's still small,

03:28.800 --> 03:31.060
as long as it has
a strong will to 'survive',

03:31.980 --> 03:35.260
anyone would be

03:35.260 --> 03:37.260
any kind of situation.

03:37.660 --> 03:40.480
That's the animal 'instinct'.

03:40.920 --> 03:43.480
To save a life out of sympathy

03:43.480 --> 03:46.300
can sometimes bring tragic outcomes.

03:46.860 --> 03:50.480
This puppy is an animal
that was abandoned.

03:50.480 --> 03:53.280
It is not needed by anyone.

03:53.680 --> 03:55.900
If such fragile creatures

03:55.900 --> 03:58.740
do not become stronger on their own,

03:58.740 --> 04:01.320
they will inevitably die
on the roadside someday.

04:02.020 --> 04:04.420
If you save its life
without consideration,

04:04.420 --> 04:09.460
that responsibility may turn into
a danger and befall you one day.

04:10.240 --> 04:13.920
Master Hitoyoshi, can you truly
bear this responsibility?

04:14.460 --> 04:16.180
Um…

04:16.860 --> 04:19.840
I don't quite understand that.

04:20.480 --> 04:24.220
You didn't save my life yesterday

04:25.980 --> 04:27.840
out of sympathy, right?

04:30.120 --> 04:34.820
When there is a life to be saved,
the body acts before the mind.

04:34.820 --> 04:37.120
This must be a human instinct.

04:37.640 --> 04:40.620
'Human' instinct.

04:41.080 --> 04:42.320
Moreover,

04:42.320 --> 04:45.960
I understand the feeling
of being abandoned.

04:47.220 --> 04:50.200
Anyway, let's not stand here talking.

04:50.200 --> 04:52.580
Throw away the trash and go home.

04:52.860 --> 04:56.700
It's so hot that we could get roasted.

05:00.260 --> 05:03.160
You're so friendly and cute.

05:03.820 --> 05:05.460
Miss Maid, would you
like to try holding it?

05:05.460 --> 05:07.360
Um… I…

05:07.880 --> 05:09.360
I'll pass.

05:09.800 --> 05:11.200
Why are you backing away so much?

05:11.740 --> 05:13.060
I am not…

05:13.060 --> 05:14.520
Look, it's all fluffy.

05:19.440 --> 05:21.520
Miss Maid, could it be that…

05:21.520 --> 05:23.080
you're afraid of dogs?

05:24.340 --> 05:26.160
No, um…

05:27.200 --> 05:29.360
Just a tiny bit.

05:30.040 --> 05:34.460
Really… just a little bit… afraid of it…

05:34.960 --> 05:36.360
So cute.

05:37.020 --> 05:38.480
But…

05:38.480 --> 05:40.400
If it's an order,

05:40.400 --> 05:42.660
if Master Hitoyoshi wants me to hold it…

05:42.660 --> 05:44.960
You don't have to force yourself.

05:45.600 --> 05:47.320
Why are you afraid?

05:49.240 --> 05:52.320
I have someone who I could call a teacher.

05:52.320 --> 05:55.860
When I was young,
under the name of training,

05:55.860 --> 05:59.580
he left me in the deep mountains
with many fierce wild dogs.

06:00.300 --> 06:02.620
No wonder you have trauma.

06:03.160 --> 06:06.160
In that case, it would be difficult
for you to take care of it.

06:06.160 --> 06:11.060
That's a headache.

06:12.320 --> 06:14.740
I… I'm really sorry…

06:15.160 --> 06:16.820
that I can't help…

06:16.820 --> 06:19.300
Ah, I'm not blaming you.

06:19.300 --> 06:20.620
It's just…

06:20.620 --> 06:23.600
I don't want to leave it alone anymore.

06:23.600 --> 06:26.660
So I might have to ask you
to endure it for a while.

06:28.060 --> 06:30.180
Even if I try to find someone to adopt it,

06:30.180 --> 06:32.380
it won't be that easy.

06:32.380 --> 06:35.460
And it's not good to just throw
the problem at someone else.

06:38.800 --> 06:40.680
Master Hitoyoshi.

06:41.100 --> 06:45.260
Can I try to hold it after all?

06:47.100 --> 06:48.380
Miss Maid.

06:48.380 --> 06:50.400
I am very grateful for your kindness.

06:50.820 --> 06:52.080
Um…

06:52.760 --> 06:55.480
You really don't have to force yourself.

06:55.900 --> 07:00.060
I am not… forcing…

07:00.060 --> 07:02.700
It's actually quite well-behaved.

07:02.700 --> 07:04.420
What exactly do you find scary?

07:04.900 --> 07:06.380
What…

07:06.720 --> 07:08.620
The sharp claws.

07:08.620 --> 07:10.220
Fierce fangs.

07:10.220 --> 07:12.000
Piercing eyes.

07:12.560 --> 07:14.060
Those are probably it.

07:14.420 --> 07:17.940
Sorry, no matter how I look at it,
it just seems like a mochi to me.

07:17.940 --> 07:19.180
Mochi?

07:19.440 --> 07:20.880
You mean

07:20.880 --> 07:23.120
that thing made out of rice?

07:23.120 --> 07:24.420
Right.

07:28.820 --> 07:31.820
Well, my opinion
should be in the majority.

07:40.060 --> 07:41.880
That was just a light bite.

07:41.880 --> 07:43.360
It wasn't really biting.

07:43.360 --> 07:46.020
Calm down. You can't throw it.

07:48.380 --> 07:50.980
Luckily you made it through.

07:51.600 --> 07:54.840
I'm really sorry for showing
such an embarrassing side of me.

07:54.840 --> 07:55.780
Hmm?

07:55.780 --> 07:59.300
Ah, are your teeth itchy?

08:04.420 --> 08:06.220
You mustn't do something so dangerous.

08:06.220 --> 08:07.900
It's okay.

08:08.240 --> 08:09.360
Good.

08:09.360 --> 08:11.180
Then let's go out.

08:12.240 --> 08:13.420
Yes.

08:16.940 --> 08:18.900
PET SHOP, ANIMAL HOSPITAL
Animal Hospital…

08:18.900 --> 08:19.560
PET SHOP, ANIMAL HOSPITAL
Hmm.

08:19.940 --> 08:21.300
Although it looks very spirited,

08:21.300 --> 08:24.000
I still think it'd be better
to bring it in for a check-up.

08:33.680 --> 08:36.480
Miss Maid, could you please take
a look at the mall next door for me?

08:36.700 --> 08:37.740
Okay.

08:37.740 --> 08:40.700
DOG FOOD, DENTAL BONE

08:48.680 --> 08:51.900
She's picking very carefully for you.

08:51.900 --> 08:53.460
Are you happy?

08:59.880 --> 09:01.540
Thank you, Miss Maid.

09:01.860 --> 09:04.920
You picked all the necessary items for me.

09:06.340 --> 09:09.900
Master Hitoyoshi, you're really gentle.

09:09.900 --> 09:10.800
Huh?

09:11.600 --> 09:16.640
Never before in my life have I encountered
someone like you.

09:17.160 --> 09:21.380
The place where I lived
did not tolerate any failure.

09:22.480 --> 09:23.920
Perhaps that is exactly why

09:24.640 --> 09:26.900
whenever I am treated gently,

09:28.260 --> 09:32.400
I feel the distance between you and me.

09:33.120 --> 09:34.460
For a long time,

09:34.860 --> 09:38.240
all I had to do was complete the tasks.

09:39.000 --> 09:41.400
But your requests

09:41.400 --> 09:44.120
are all new to me.

09:44.900 --> 09:47.660
Many times it's been in vain

09:48.000 --> 09:49.230
and ended in failure.

09:50.740 --> 09:54.380
I really don't know

09:55.180 --> 10:01.280
how to become someone you need.

10:03.140 --> 10:04.360
In the past,

10:04.760 --> 10:08.520
there were times
I've been deemed unneeded.

10:10.160 --> 10:14.120
The world I belonged to was like a game

10:14.120 --> 10:16.280
where we fought for
the few chairs available.

10:16.840 --> 10:19.580
We are the pawns of the powerful.

10:19.580 --> 10:22.900
As long as one has the ability,
age and gender do not matter.

10:23.780 --> 10:25.480
To secure my place to survive,

10:28.580 --> 10:31.500
there was only one thing I must do.

10:32.240 --> 10:34.230
YOKOYA
However, it's not like that here.

10:34.920 --> 10:37.160
What I can do

10:37.160 --> 10:39.300
and what I have done

10:39.300 --> 10:41.020
only bring limited achievements.

10:42.420 --> 10:46.880
If I could meet you like that puppy,

10:47.740 --> 10:54.020
if I could know that
the world is full of warmth,

10:55.400 --> 11:00.020
perhaps I could become what you wish for.

11:01.180 --> 11:03.980
Can I stay here

11:04.700 --> 11:07.340
in this dazzling world?

11:07.340 --> 11:10.300
Am I really needed?

11:11.020 --> 11:12.780
Miss Maid…

11:12.780 --> 11:14.020
Oh!

11:14.020 --> 11:16.820
Don't pull me while I'm talking.

11:18.680 --> 11:20.340
Miss Maid,

11:20.340 --> 11:23.140
you must want to give up your previous job

11:23.520 --> 11:24.990
and become a normal girl.

11:26.520 --> 11:28.580
Give up killing?

11:28.940 --> 11:31.380
That's what it sounds like to me.

11:32.740 --> 11:33.960
Wait…

11:33.960 --> 11:36.900
No, it's all tangled up now.

11:37.300 --> 11:40.340
-Hey, don't run around.
-Give up being an assassin… become normal…

11:43.320 --> 11:45.680
I never thought about it.

11:46.500 --> 11:49.900
Killing was my only reason for existence.

11:50.440 --> 11:52.600
That's what I was taught.

11:52.600 --> 11:56.400
So that someone like me
could also be needed,

11:56.840 --> 12:00.400
I could only keep killing

12:00.400 --> 12:02.620
on this path of slaughter.

12:03.620 --> 12:04.680
But…

12:04.680 --> 12:05.860
If…

12:05.860 --> 12:07.080
Wow.

12:07.680 --> 12:10.160
The sunset is so beautiful.

12:22.180 --> 12:26.980
If I could find a place to belong
other than in killing…

12:27.640 --> 12:30.480
Can I understand more

12:30.940 --> 12:34.840
about this master

12:35.260 --> 12:37.960
and this dazzling and warm world?

12:39.600 --> 12:43.100
When you first came to my house,

12:43.100 --> 12:45.980
I was really scared of you.

12:47.400 --> 12:50.600
Because no one around me is an assassin.

12:51.140 --> 12:54.580
But after spending time with you,

12:54.580 --> 12:56.180
I realized you are not what I thought.

12:57.520 --> 13:00.700
You're in fact a good kid.

13:01.720 --> 13:03.120
Good kid.

13:04.880 --> 13:06.160
Good kid…

13:13.540 --> 13:15.160
Master Hitoyoshi.

13:15.760 --> 13:17.580
If I want to become a 'normal' girl,

13:17.580 --> 13:19.500
what should I do?

13:19.500 --> 13:20.520
Eh…

13:21.080 --> 13:24.020
Eh, this is a difficult question.

13:24.420 --> 13:26.100
Ah, there is one thing though.

13:26.560 --> 13:30.360
You seem to be very concerned
about your failures.

13:30.360 --> 13:32.300
But you said it yourself, didn't you?

13:32.300 --> 13:35.280
After you came here,
everything you encountered was new to you.

13:36.020 --> 13:37.620
If you're doing it for the first time,

13:37.620 --> 13:40.980
it's 'normal' to
experience failure, right?

13:55.320 --> 14:00.440
Indeed, cutting it this way allows for
efficient and even shredding of the cabbage.

14:00.440 --> 14:02.680
And there's no need
to concentrate intensely.

14:03.180 --> 14:06.840
What's called 'normal'
might just refer to efficiency.

14:07.500 --> 14:09.080
Okonomiyaki…

14:09.080 --> 14:10.800
I don't know what kind of food it is.

14:11.140 --> 14:14.120
I heard it's a dish mainly based on sauce.

14:14.660 --> 14:16.960
It seems not to be fried food.

14:16.960 --> 14:19.160
But it does use cabbage.

14:19.520 --> 14:22.540
Cabbage indeed seems
to pair well with sauce…

14:26.280 --> 14:27.240
Impossible!

14:27.240 --> 14:29.740
I was approached from behind!

14:30.020 --> 14:31.520
You…

14:32.220 --> 14:34.020
You're not an ordinary dog after all.

14:37.080 --> 14:38.520
You…

14:38.860 --> 14:40.860
You are hungry?

14:44.120 --> 14:46.420
Being able to understand other's feelings.

14:46.780 --> 14:49.700
It's also a part of being normal, right?

14:57.220 --> 14:58.560
I'm back.

14:59.160 --> 15:00.440
What's wrong?

15:00.820 --> 15:01.900
Nothing…

15:02.120 --> 15:04.620
Ah, you fed it, huh?

15:04.620 --> 15:05.660
Thank you.

15:05.660 --> 15:06.560
Yes…

15:06.560 --> 15:09.060
That's great, is it tasty?

15:10.420 --> 15:12.060
You really can eat a lot.

15:12.060 --> 15:13.380
Is that okay?

15:13.380 --> 15:16.100
Your belly is super soft and squishy.

15:16.100 --> 15:18.320
As soft as mochi.

15:18.600 --> 15:21.020
Mochi…

15:22.700 --> 15:24.020
I have an idea.

15:24.780 --> 15:26.400
Your name

15:26.400 --> 15:27.400
will be Agemochitarou.

15:27.400 --> 15:28.280
MOCHI IS DELICIOUS!
will be Agemochitarou.

15:29.120 --> 15:30.080
How is it?

15:32.020 --> 15:34.120
I think it's a great name.

15:35.640 --> 15:38.980
Oh, you like it too?

15:38.980 --> 15:43.320
It's simple, and more importantly,
it has an imposing aura.

15:44.060 --> 15:45.240
Is that so?

15:45.880 --> 15:47.800
You've shredded the cabbage for me.

15:47.800 --> 15:49.820
Thank you, you've been a great help.

15:49.820 --> 15:51.800
Not, it's nothing…

15:52.300 --> 15:54.080
Regarding the maid's work,

15:54.520 --> 15:56.140
you've become quite adept at it.

15:58.500 --> 16:00.480
Leave the rest to me.

16:00.900 --> 16:03.440
Oh, what's wrong, Agemochitarou?

16:03.440 --> 16:05.080
Do you want to play with me?

16:05.360 --> 16:08.400
Sorry, I can only play
with you after dinner.

16:09.840 --> 16:11.120
Hey, hey.

16:11.120 --> 16:12.960
I'll take care of it.

16:12.960 --> 16:14.820
Eh, is that okay?

16:14.820 --> 16:16.340
You don't have to force yourself…

16:16.340 --> 16:17.820
No problem.

16:18.360 --> 16:21.440
I want to become 'normal'.

16:22.180 --> 16:24.780
Master Hitoyoshi, you said

16:24.780 --> 16:27.400
that the puppy is very well-behaved.

16:27.740 --> 16:29.020
But,

16:29.020 --> 16:33.940
in my eyes, it is still
an extremely fierce wild dog.

16:34.400 --> 16:37.600
However, my notion of 'normal'

16:37.600 --> 16:40.540
is everything you have said.

16:40.940 --> 16:44.080
This fear cannot be removed.

16:44.480 --> 16:45.820
But even so,

16:46.860 --> 16:48.380
I still want to believe

16:48.800 --> 16:50.640
what you have said.

16:53.500 --> 16:55.060
Miss Maid…

16:56.160 --> 16:58.880
Then, I also believe in you.

16:58.880 --> 17:02.200
Believe in you…

17:03.360 --> 17:04.560
Yes.

17:04.560 --> 17:05.880
You can leave it to me.

17:21.560 --> 17:23.440
Can I hold it?

17:23.440 --> 17:24.620
Of course.

17:32.760 --> 17:34.740
This is Mochi?

17:34.740 --> 17:36.460
That's just a metaphor.

17:36.460 --> 17:37.860
It's a dog.

17:38.260 --> 17:41.000
Small and warm.

17:43.400 --> 17:46.440
I was really scared of you.

17:46.440 --> 17:49.620
But after spending time with you,

17:49.620 --> 17:51.220
I realized you are not what I thought.

17:51.600 --> 17:54.700
You're in fact a good kid.

17:55.720 --> 17:58.100
I understand now too.

17:58.100 --> 17:59.280
Hmm?

17:59.580 --> 18:02.880
It's quite embarrassing
to be ever-fearful.

18:09.100 --> 18:10.610
KATSUTA SAUCE

18:13.480 --> 18:14.880
Okonomiyaki…

18:14.880 --> 18:16.060
Delicious…

18:16.060 --> 18:18.100
That sauce… sauce…

18:18.100 --> 18:19.760
With this noodle crust…

18:19.760 --> 18:22.160
Cabbage and sauce together…

18:22.160 --> 18:24.940
She's suddenly talking
like a kindergartener.

18:26.580 --> 18:28.560
Okonomiyaki.

18:28.560 --> 18:29.760
It's truly delicious.

18:30.820 --> 18:32.400
So, would you like another one?

18:33.740 --> 18:36.860
But I can't trouble you any further.

18:37.200 --> 18:39.260
Your body is quite honest, though.

18:39.260 --> 18:40.320
OKONOMIYAKI POWDER

18:40.320 --> 18:43.760
It's normal to say willful things
about what you like.

18:44.980 --> 18:46.100
So,

18:46.100 --> 18:49.360
it's also normal to want
another serving of okonomiyaki.

18:50.100 --> 18:53.080
Then I'll humbly comply.

18:53.700 --> 18:57.200
If you have any other willful requests,
don't hesitate to speak up.

18:57.200 --> 18:58.860
Willful…

18:59.760 --> 19:04.180
This is a special service for you
who have gotten closer with Agemochitarou.

19:06.260 --> 19:07.740
In that case,

19:08.360 --> 19:10.620
I'd also like to ask you

19:10.620 --> 19:13.080
to give me a name, Master Hitoyoshi.

19:13.080 --> 19:15.720
You want me to choose a name for you?

19:15.720 --> 19:16.920
Yes.

19:16.920 --> 19:18.720
Something like Agemochitarou…

19:18.720 --> 19:23.000
Well, giving you such a name
doesn't seem quite right.

19:23.340 --> 19:24.560
Hmm…

19:24.560 --> 19:27.540
To choose a name for you…

19:28.500 --> 19:30.680
When is your birthday?

19:30.680 --> 19:33.400
Although I don't know the exact date,

19:33.400 --> 19:35.380
it appears to be a freezing winter.

19:35.380 --> 19:38.500
I was born on a record-breaking snowy day.

19:38.500 --> 19:41.160
I have faint memories of
hearing others say so.

19:41.160 --> 19:42.260
Winter.

19:42.260 --> 19:44.220
Born in winter, huh?

19:44.220 --> 19:47.200
Then, how about 'Miss Yuki'?

19:48.340 --> 19:51.300
You're a cold-blooded killer.

19:51.300 --> 19:52.680
'Snow'.

19:53.720 --> 19:57.100
I, for one, really like snow.

19:57.100 --> 19:59.100
It's white and beautiful.

19:59.760 --> 20:02.740
Don't you get excited
when you see the snow falling?

20:04.700 --> 20:07.440
Moreover, snow is very warm.

20:07.700 --> 20:09.800
It is?

20:09.800 --> 20:11.640
This is what I've heard.

20:12.080 --> 20:14.280
If the fields are covered with snow,

20:14.280 --> 20:17.340
the soil and seeds beneath it
can survive the winter without freezing.

20:17.340 --> 20:19.600
When spring comes,
new buds will grow again.

20:19.600 --> 20:23.940
Isn't it the snow protecting them,
keeping them warm?

20:27.860 --> 20:32.320
Why did my body start moving on its own?

20:33.140 --> 20:37.320
Why does this world feel so warm?

20:37.900 --> 20:42.880
Why does this person touch my heart?

20:46.360 --> 20:48.460
If I stay here

20:48.820 --> 20:51.240
living with this person,

20:51.840 --> 20:56.860
I feel that one day I will understand.

20:59.420 --> 21:00.660
Yuki.

21:01.020 --> 21:03.880
